1
00:00:01,251 --> 00:00:03,629
[Cheery instrumental music]

2
00:00:04,505 --> 00:00:06,048
LOIS: Look at Stewie.

3
00:00:06,131 --> 00:00:09,301
Isn't he adorable
playing with his Sesame Street phone?

4
00:00:09,384 --> 00:00:11,053
Put me through to the Pentagon.

5
00:00:11,136 --> 00:00:14,139
ERNIE: What sound does a cow make?
STEWIE: Don't toy with me!

6
00:00:14,223 --> 00:00:16,225
I've already dispatched with Mr. Hooper.

7
00:00:16,308 --> 00:00:18,352
I've six armed men outside
Big Bird's nest.

8
00:00:18,435 --> 00:00:20,187
And as for Linda?

9
00:00:20,270 --> 00:00:23,649
It's difficult for a deaf woman
to hear an assassin approach, isn't it?

10
00:00:23,732 --> 00:00:26,527
ERNIE: Can you count to three?
STEWIE: Indeed I can.

11
00:00:26,610 --> 00:00:28,862
One! Two! Three!

12
00:00:29,696 --> 00:00:31,823
Can I count to three? For God's sake,

13
00:00:31,907 --> 00:00:34,034
I'm already shooting
at a fifth-grade level.

14
00:00:34,535 --> 00:00:37,746
LOIS: [Singing]
"It seems today that all you see

15
00:00:37,829 --> 00:00:41,166
"is violence in movies and sex on TV

16
00:00:41,250 --> 00:00:44,628
"But where are those good,
old-fashioned values

17
00:00:44,878 --> 00:00:47,548
"on which we used to rely?

18
00:00:48,048 --> 00:00:50,843
"Lucky there's a family guy

19
00:00:51,301 --> 00:00:54,471
"Lucky there's a man who'll
positively tell you

20
00:00:54,555 --> 00:00:56,181
"all the things that make us

21
00:00:56,265 --> 00:00:57,808
"laugh 'n' cry

22
00:00:57,891 --> 00:01:02,813
"He's a family guy"

23
00:01:05,858 --> 00:01:06,859
Come on, Stewie.

24
00:01:06,942 --> 00:01:09,820
You can't leave the table
until you finish your vegetables.

25
00:01:09,903 --> 00:01:12,239
Then I shall sit here until
one of us expires.

26
00:01:12,322 --> 00:01:14,616
You've got a good 40 years on me, woman!

27
00:01:14,700 --> 00:01:19,746
Sweetie, it's broccoli. It's good
for you. Now open up for the airplane.

28
00:01:19,830 --> 00:01:21,081
[Makes airplane noise]

29
00:01:21,164 --> 00:01:24,418
Never! Damn the broccoli! Damn you!
And damn the Wright Brothers!

30
00:01:24,501 --> 00:01:28,839
My, aren't we fussy tonight.
Okay. No broccoli.

31
00:01:29,131 --> 00:01:30,924
Very well then. I--

32
00:01:31,967 --> 00:01:33,927
Who the hell do you think you are?

33
00:01:34,011 --> 00:01:37,222
Honey, it's not gonna go away
just because you don't like it.

34
00:01:37,306 --> 00:01:41,602
Well, then. My goal becomes clear.
The broccoli must die.

35
00:01:41,935 --> 00:01:44,062
[Sinister instrumental music]

36
00:01:45,814 --> 00:01:47,858
Mom, will you take me out
to practice driving?

37
00:01:47,941 --> 00:01:50,110
I'm teaching a piano lesson
in half an hour.

38
00:01:50,194 --> 00:01:52,362
Maybe your father can take you.

39
00:01:52,446 --> 00:01:55,824
Sorry, Meg. Daddy loves you.
But Daddy also loves Star Trek.

40
00:01:55,908 --> 00:01:58,493
And, in all fairness,
Star Trek was here first.

41
00:01:58,994 --> 00:02:01,747
KIRK: Captain's log, Stardate 8169.7.

42
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:05,334
The Enterprise has just discovered
a strange new planet...

43
00:02:05,417 --> 00:02:08,670
...in the Gamma Faloppia star system.
Mr. Sulu, ahead Warp 9.

44
00:02:09,755 --> 00:02:11,048
LOIS: For God's sake, Peter.

45
00:02:11,131 --> 00:02:14,009
You've been in front of the TV
since you got home from work.

46
00:02:14,092 --> 00:02:16,428
Why don't you spend some time
with your family?

47
00:02:16,512 --> 00:02:18,722
I will, during the commercials.

48
00:02:18,805 --> 00:02:22,476
And if that's wrong, maybe I'm missing
the point of having commercials.

49
00:02:22,559 --> 00:02:23,560
[Sighs]

50
00:02:23,644 --> 00:02:26,980
Please. My road test is tomorrow
and you haven't taught me anything.

51
00:02:27,064 --> 00:02:29,274
You may want to find
a better teacher than Peter.

52
00:02:29,358 --> 00:02:31,652
What are you talking about?
I'm a great driver.

53
00:02:31,735 --> 00:02:33,237
Remember your trip to the Southwest?

54
00:02:34,238 --> 00:02:35,322
[Road Runner meep-meeping]

55
00:02:37,783 --> 00:02:39,993
-Jeez. Did I just hit that ostrich?
-No.

56
00:02:40,077 --> 00:02:41,787
-Are you sure?
-He's fine. Keep going.

57
00:02:41,995 --> 00:02:44,790
Don't believe that.
I always keep my eyes on the road.

58
00:02:44,873 --> 00:02:47,584
PETER: I don't miss a thing.
TV: We now return to Star Trek.

59
00:02:47,668 --> 00:02:49,336
Holy crap. Uhura's black?

60
00:02:51,588 --> 00:02:53,632
All right, Meg.
Now here's your first lesson.

61
00:02:53,715 --> 00:02:56,176
You always want to be aware
of other cars on the road.

62
00:02:56,260 --> 00:03:00,639
If you catch eyes with the guy next to you
at a red light, you gotta race him.

63
00:03:04,434 --> 00:03:06,228
-This guy's asking for it.
-But Dad....

64
00:03:06,311 --> 00:03:09,398
I don't make the rules, honey.
Now rev your engine twice.

65
00:03:09,481 --> 00:03:10,607
Okay.

66
00:03:10,732 --> 00:03:12,317
[Engine revving twice]

67
00:03:12,734 --> 00:03:14,236
[Horse sputtering twice]

68
00:03:14,528 --> 00:03:15,529
Go!

69
00:03:16,029 --> 00:03:18,282
[Fast-paced instrumental music]

70
00:03:21,451 --> 00:03:22,619
[Screaming]

71
00:03:22,703 --> 00:03:24,621
[Dramatic instrumental music]

72
00:03:28,333 --> 00:03:31,962
PETER: You forgot to flip him off.
But other than that, nice job.

73
00:03:33,130 --> 00:03:35,632
You're back already?
That wasn't much of a lesson.

74
00:03:35,716 --> 00:03:38,260
I didn't want to overload her
on her first time out.

75
00:03:38,343 --> 00:03:40,053
Besides CHiPs is about to start.

76
00:03:40,137 --> 00:03:45,142
So let's sit back and get lost in a world
of California Highway Patrol fantasy!

77
00:03:45,559 --> 00:03:46,560
[Police siren]

78
00:03:46,643 --> 00:03:48,520
[Funky instrumental music]

79
00:03:48,604 --> 00:03:52,065
-What's the charge, Officer?
-Driving without my phone number.

80
00:03:55,569 --> 00:03:57,237
[Gunshots firing]

81
00:03:57,613 --> 00:04:00,449
Or maybe I should arrest you
for being too beautiful.

82
00:04:00,532 --> 00:04:01,617
[Teeth sparkling]

83
00:04:03,285 --> 00:04:05,913
So, broccoli, Mother says
you're very good for me.

84
00:04:05,996 --> 00:04:10,083
I'm afraid I'm no good for you!
The first rule of war is know thine enemy.

85
00:04:10,167 --> 00:04:13,962
And I know this! Cold kills broccoli!
It's so simple.

86
00:04:14,463 --> 00:04:17,883
All I need to do is build a machine
to control the global environment.

87
00:04:17,966 --> 00:04:22,304
Forecast for tomorrow, a few sprinkles
of genius with a chance of doom!

88
00:04:22,387 --> 00:04:23,764
[Sinister instrumental music]

89
00:04:26,266 --> 00:04:27,726
PETER: This is taking forever!

90
00:04:27,809 --> 00:04:31,313
Come on. Let's go. Fox is running
one of those new reality shows at 8:00.

91
00:04:31,396 --> 00:04:33,398
Fast Animals, Slow Children.

92
00:04:33,565 --> 00:04:35,317
[African instrumental music]

93
00:04:35,526 --> 00:04:37,486
Come on, guys. Wait up.

94
00:04:37,569 --> 00:04:39,238
[African music continues]

95
00:04:39,905 --> 00:04:42,324
Dang. I got honey all over my legs.

96
00:04:43,867 --> 00:04:47,579
Dad, we can't leave now. My entire life
depends on getting my license.

97
00:04:47,663 --> 00:04:50,916
If I can't drive, I'll never have
a boyfriend, never get married...

98
00:04:50,999 --> 00:04:54,586
...and then I'll have to adopt a kid
like Rosie O'Donnell.

99
00:04:54,670 --> 00:04:57,089
Are you implying
that Rosie O'Donnell can't drive?

100
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:01,218
I'm so nervous.

101
00:05:01,301 --> 00:05:03,971
You're gonna do great.
Remember everything I taught you.

102
00:05:06,056 --> 00:05:08,809
-Let's start by going down Main Street.
-Okay.

103
00:05:14,815 --> 00:05:16,275
[Engine revving twice]

104
00:05:17,568 --> 00:05:18,569
[Police siren]

105
00:05:18,652 --> 00:05:21,113
-What are you doing?
-I'm driving.

106
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:25,742
[Screaming]

107
00:05:26,994 --> 00:05:29,621
Are you gonna mark me down
for not flipping him off?

108
00:05:30,706 --> 00:05:35,002
God, my life is over.
I am the biggest loser I know!

109
00:05:35,085 --> 00:05:38,672
I know how you feel, pumpkin.
I've had my share of disappointments, too.

110
00:05:38,964 --> 00:05:40,382
DOCTOR: It's a girl!

111
00:05:40,966 --> 00:05:42,718
Can you check again?

112
00:05:43,302 --> 00:05:46,680
You just have to remember that life
has its little ups and.... Jeez!

113
00:05:46,763 --> 00:05:50,267
We're gonna miss the beginning
of my show. There it is.

114
00:05:51,768 --> 00:05:52,769
MEG: Dad, watch out!

115
00:05:52,853 --> 00:05:53,854
[Horn blaring]

116
00:06:07,034 --> 00:06:10,621
PETER: Meg, honey, are you okay?
MEG: Yeah, I think so.

117
00:06:12,623 --> 00:06:15,375
PETER: The Quahog
Cable Television Transmitter.

118
00:06:16,835 --> 00:06:18,420
[Citizens grumbling]

119
00:06:18,837 --> 00:06:21,507
You just knocked out cable TV
for the whole town!

120
00:06:21,590 --> 00:06:24,051
Boy! Look. There's Bigfoot!

121
00:06:24,593 --> 00:06:27,095
Whoa. This isn't about me.
This is about you.

122
00:06:27,179 --> 00:06:28,931
At least I bought us some time.

123
00:06:29,806 --> 00:06:32,893
-She did it.
-What? Dad, you were the one driving!

124
00:06:32,976 --> 00:06:36,730
I was teaching her to drive
and she lost control of the car.

125
00:06:36,855 --> 00:06:39,900
Come on, we all did stupid stuff
when we were kids, right?

126
00:06:39,983 --> 00:06:42,611
I remember when I tried
to sneak into an R-rated movie.

127
00:06:46,406 --> 00:06:49,034
-Come on. Give the kid a break, huh?
-Why should we?

128
00:06:50,661 --> 00:06:52,496
She got her arm shot off in Vietnam.

129
00:06:52,579 --> 00:06:53,580
[Murmuring]

130
00:06:53,664 --> 00:06:55,624
GUY: Poor kid.
MAN: What a senseless war.

131
00:06:56,124 --> 00:06:58,669
I can't believe you just sold out
your own daughter.

132
00:06:58,752 --> 00:07:01,004
I know what I did was wrong. And I know

133
00:07:01,088 --> 00:07:03,382
it's not the first time
I've embarrassed you.

134
00:07:03,632 --> 00:07:07,219
And if you add the measure of the angles
of a right triangle, the sum--

135
00:07:07,302 --> 00:07:10,180
Meg, clean out the shower
the next time you shave your legs.

136
00:07:10,264 --> 00:07:12,099
It's like a carpet in there.

137
00:07:13,392 --> 00:07:15,519
I hate to see you so upset.

138
00:07:15,936 --> 00:07:20,190
I know. Let's play a little game
called Taking the Fall for Daddy.

139
00:07:20,274 --> 00:07:23,235
If you win, I'll buy you a convertible
when you get your license.

140
00:07:23,318 --> 00:07:26,822
Really? Daddy! Now I love you again!

141
00:07:27,114 --> 00:07:29,783
You're gonna make
some Jewish guy a great wife.

142
00:07:29,867 --> 00:07:31,076
[Metallic clanking]

143
00:07:33,370 --> 00:07:35,831
Because of an accident
at the Quahog Cable Company...

144
00:07:35,914 --> 00:07:39,418
...television transmission will be out
for an undetermined amount of time.

145
00:07:39,501 --> 00:07:41,628
Of course, no one can see
this news program...

146
00:07:41,712 --> 00:07:45,007
...so it doesn't really matter
what we say. I'm the Lord Jesus Christ.

147
00:07:45,090 --> 00:07:47,801
Think I'll go get drunk and
beat up midgets. How about you?

148
00:07:47,926 --> 00:07:50,721
Tom, I just plain don't like black people.

149
00:07:51,388 --> 00:07:53,891
You guys, we're still on in Boston.

150
00:07:58,103 --> 00:08:01,148
Excellent.
The weather machine is nearly completed.

151
00:08:01,231 --> 00:08:03,650
What do you say to that, broccoli?

152
00:08:04,526 --> 00:08:07,529
Stop mocking me! What's this?

153
00:08:07,613 --> 00:08:11,283
It appears the witless provider
has finally brought me something of value.

154
00:08:11,366 --> 00:08:14,786
I can use that crude device
to amplify my deadly signal.

155
00:08:14,870 --> 00:08:16,914
Victory shall yet be mine.

156
00:08:17,748 --> 00:08:18,749
Guess what, Mom?

157
00:08:18,832 --> 00:08:21,126
Dad crashed the car
into the city cable transmitter.

158
00:08:21,210 --> 00:08:22,586
-What?
-It's okay.

159
00:08:22,669 --> 00:08:26,089
If I take the blame, he'll buy me
a convertible when I get my license.

160
00:08:26,173 --> 00:08:30,636
Meg, it's not exactly taking the blame
if you go around telling everyone.

161
00:08:30,886 --> 00:08:33,514
Peter, you're bribing your daughter
with a car?

162
00:08:33,597 --> 00:08:34,973
Come on, Lois.

163
00:08:35,057 --> 00:08:37,059
Isn't "bribe" just another
word for "love"?

164
00:08:37,142 --> 00:08:39,144
You wanted me and Meg to bond.

165
00:08:39,228 --> 00:08:40,479
That's what we're doing.

166
00:08:40,562 --> 00:08:43,148
CHRIS: Dad, I was in a chat room
on America Online...

167
00:08:43,232 --> 00:08:46,902
...and Doomie 22 told me
some idiot knocked out the cable.

168
00:08:46,985 --> 00:08:49,112
We could be without TV for weeks!

169
00:08:49,196 --> 00:08:52,699
Now, Chris, now let's not panic.
We can manage just fine without TV.

170
00:08:52,783 --> 00:08:53,784
[Brian scoffs]

171
00:08:53,867 --> 00:08:57,287
-What's that supposed to mean?
-Face it, you're addicted to television.

172
00:08:57,371 --> 00:09:00,624
You're not exactly Mr. Cold Turkey.
Remember when you gave up candy?

173
00:09:01,083 --> 00:09:04,628
I'll ask you one more time.
You didn't eat anything in my factory?

174
00:09:04,878 --> 00:09:05,879
No.

175
00:09:05,963 --> 00:09:08,048
-I'm just asking--
-Are you calling me a liar?

176
00:09:08,131 --> 00:09:09,883
-I'm just saying--
-Shut up, Wonka.

177
00:09:10,175 --> 00:09:12,094
Yeah. That was different. I'll be fine.

178
00:09:12,177 --> 00:09:14,847
-Are you sure, honey?
-For God's sake, you guys.

179
00:09:14,930 --> 00:09:18,433
You think I'm some simp who can't live
without TV? Give me a break.

180
00:09:18,767 --> 00:09:20,519
What's happening now?

181
00:09:20,602 --> 00:09:22,354
Sipowicz is finding who
stabbed the super.

182
00:09:22,437 --> 00:09:25,440
Are you gonna tell me,
or am I gonna have to show you my ass?

183
00:09:25,566 --> 00:09:28,068
I ain't saying nothing!
All right, it was Jimmy the Hat!

184
00:09:28,485 --> 00:09:29,736
Forget it, Mike.

185
00:09:29,820 --> 00:09:32,614
Without actually seeing his ass,
this is just radio.

186
00:09:34,366 --> 00:09:38,620
Class, we were scheduled to watch
a PBS program on the mating rituals...

187
00:09:38,704 --> 00:09:41,582
...of the nude large-breasted Weewok tribe
of New Guinea.

188
00:09:41,665 --> 00:09:45,043
Unfortunately, Megan Griffin ruined TV.

189
00:09:45,419 --> 00:09:48,046
So instead, we're having a surprise test.

190
00:09:48,130 --> 00:09:51,216
WONDER YEARS VOICE: Suddenly I was
public enemy number one.

191
00:09:51,633 --> 00:09:53,302
It was time to tell the truth.

192
00:09:53,719 --> 00:09:56,763
Wait! I didn't drive into
the satellite dish!

193
00:09:56,847 --> 00:09:58,348
And who did?

194
00:09:58,432 --> 00:10:00,767
WONDER YEARS VOICE:
I was just a 15-year-old girl.

195
00:10:01,351 --> 00:10:05,397
But at that moment, I realized I had
a whole lifetime to make new friends.

196
00:10:05,480 --> 00:10:09,443
But only one chance to get a new car.
And I had to take it.

197
00:10:09,735 --> 00:10:11,236
Okay, I did it.

198
00:10:13,614 --> 00:10:16,033
PETER: I don't know how much longer
I can last.

199
00:10:16,116 --> 00:10:18,994
It's been a whole week
since I seen a TV show.

200
00:10:19,703 --> 00:10:21,955
I wonder what Scooby and the gang
are up to now.

201
00:10:22,039 --> 00:10:24,374
NARRATOR: We now return to
The Scooby Doo Murder Files.

202
00:10:24,791 --> 00:10:25,834
Gee whiz, gang.

203
00:10:25,918 --> 00:10:29,171
The killer gutted the victim,
strangled him with his own intestines...

204
00:10:29,254 --> 00:10:32,633
-...and then dumped the body in the river!
-Jinkies! What a mystery!

205
00:10:32,716 --> 00:10:33,759
[Moaning]

206
00:10:33,842 --> 00:10:37,137
You're right, Scoob. We're dealing
with one sick son of a bitch.

207
00:10:37,471 --> 00:10:41,141
You just need to find something
to fill the void that's left in your life.

208
00:10:41,225 --> 00:10:44,686
Lois has knitting, Chris has video games,
Meg's learning how to drive.

209
00:10:44,770 --> 00:10:46,730
And me, I like the sauce.

210
00:10:48,732 --> 00:10:51,902
Whose leg do you have to hump
to get a dry martini around here?

211
00:10:53,529 --> 00:10:54,947
[Moaning]

212
00:10:55,113 --> 00:10:59,868
Can't live without TV. Must see TV.

213
00:11:00,494 --> 00:11:02,704
[Frightful instrumental music]

214
00:11:10,963 --> 00:11:13,298
[Whimsical instrumental music]

215
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:32,526
[Sinister instrumental music]

216
00:11:32,734 --> 00:11:34,111
[Dramatic instrumental music]

217
00:11:37,239 --> 00:11:38,240
[Sighs]

218
00:11:40,868 --> 00:11:44,079
Stewie, I expect you
to finish off your vegetables.

219
00:11:44,162 --> 00:11:48,125
Rest assured, you relentless harridan,
I expect I shall finish them all off!

220
00:11:48,208 --> 00:11:49,418
And you as well!

221
00:11:49,710 --> 00:11:51,962
Brian, I'm a little worried about Peter.

222
00:11:52,045 --> 00:11:55,382
Last night I woke up and he was
channel surfing through static.

223
00:11:55,465 --> 00:11:57,926
I'm sure he'll find a way to cope.

224
00:11:59,261 --> 00:12:01,889
-Morning, Lois.
-And you were worried.

225
00:12:01,972 --> 00:12:06,143
-Peter, what the hell is that?
-It's my favorite TV family, the Griffins.

226
00:12:06,226 --> 00:12:08,312
Peter, you're scaring me. I'm beginning

227
00:12:08,395 --> 00:12:10,480
to think you're losing
your grip on reality.

228
00:12:10,564 --> 00:12:12,608
PETER: Boring.
I'll go see what else is on.

229
00:12:12,691 --> 00:12:14,693
LOIS: Peter! Keep an eye on Stewie.

230
00:12:16,069 --> 00:12:17,404
Don't move!

231
00:12:17,487 --> 00:12:19,489
[Making ridiculous noises]

232
00:12:21,950 --> 00:12:22,951
[Screams]

233
00:12:24,119 --> 00:12:25,370
STEWIE: A little help?

234
00:12:28,582 --> 00:12:31,084
PETER: It's Glen Quagmire,
the wacky next-door neighbor.

235
00:12:31,168 --> 00:12:33,962
PETER: What's he up to this time?
QUAGMIRE: I'm going to work!

236
00:12:34,546 --> 00:12:36,840
Him and his crazy get-rich-quick schemes.

237
00:12:39,051 --> 00:12:41,970
We have to find your father, Chris.
He's not well.

238
00:12:42,054 --> 00:12:46,016
I never knew anyone who went crazy
before except my invisible friend...

239
00:12:46,099 --> 00:12:47,601
...Col. Schwartz!

240
00:12:50,687 --> 00:12:52,856
I get all the channels on this thing.

241
00:12:52,940 --> 00:12:54,316
Lifetime.

242
00:12:54,733 --> 00:12:56,026
CBS.

243
00:12:56,360 --> 00:12:57,569
Hey, UPN.

244
00:12:58,403 --> 00:13:00,697
All right. 90210.

245
00:13:03,867 --> 00:13:06,662
-Dad?
-Meg, what are you doing at West Beverly?

246
00:13:06,745 --> 00:13:09,498
They're really reaching for guest stars
in the 10th season.

247
00:13:09,581 --> 00:13:11,834
Dad, what are you doing? Get out of here!

248
00:13:11,917 --> 00:13:13,836
I'm already a total
outcast because of you!

249
00:13:13,919 --> 00:13:17,214
You're just upset because you wrecked
the cable transmitter.

250
00:13:17,297 --> 00:13:21,176
I did not! Forget it.
What good is a car if I have no friends?

251
00:13:21,844 --> 00:13:24,012
I didn't wreck TV! My dad did!

252
00:13:24,429 --> 00:13:26,014
-What?
-What'd she say?

253
00:13:26,098 --> 00:13:28,350
-Peter Griffin ruined TV?
-And blamed his daughter?

254
00:13:28,433 --> 00:13:31,144
That's the lowest thing I've ever heard.

255
00:13:31,979 --> 00:13:34,398
Peter, take that thing off and come home.

256
00:13:34,481 --> 00:13:37,276
Hey, Lois. You're just in time
for the exciting conclusion.

257
00:13:37,359 --> 00:13:40,279
Looks like some boob's
about to get lynched. Let's watch.

258
00:13:40,362 --> 00:13:41,488
There they are.

259
00:13:41,572 --> 00:13:43,115
[Suspenseful instrumental music]

260
00:13:46,493 --> 00:13:49,246
That's the guy who ruined our cable.
Let's get him!

261
00:13:50,163 --> 00:13:53,667
Stop! What is wrong with you people?

262
00:13:54,168 --> 00:13:57,880
Okay, yes. My husband is responsible
for knocking out TV.

263
00:13:58,213 --> 00:13:59,923
But we should be thanking him.

264
00:14:00,007 --> 00:14:03,177
He's broken television's hypnotic spell
over us.

265
00:14:03,385 --> 00:14:05,679
Now we can see the world for what it is...

266
00:14:05,762 --> 00:14:10,309
...a beautiful place full of wonderful
things just waiting to be experienced.

267
00:14:10,392 --> 00:14:11,935
Another chick flick.

268
00:14:12,102 --> 00:14:15,189
She's right. All the hours we've wasted
on that damn idiot box.

269
00:14:15,272 --> 00:14:17,983
-I'm gonna paint my house!
-I'll build a ship in a bottle.

270
00:14:18,066 --> 00:14:20,569
I'm gonna push a hoop with a stick
down a dirt road.

271
00:14:20,652 --> 00:14:22,070
LOIS: I'll take you home, honey.

272
00:14:23,780 --> 00:14:28,368
I can't believe I let Meg take the blame.
You were right, Lois. TV is evil.

273
00:14:28,452 --> 00:14:31,246
I hear that Manson guy watches it
in jail all day long.

274
00:14:32,206 --> 00:14:34,041
If I haven't seen it, it's new to me.

275
00:14:34,458 --> 00:14:38,378
You just went a little overboard.
You need a little balance in your life.

276
00:14:38,587 --> 00:14:42,007
There are other things to appreciate
besides television.

277
00:14:42,090 --> 00:14:46,053
-You mean like this lamp?
-Yeah. Okay.

278
00:14:46,136 --> 00:14:49,598
-The lamp gives us light.
-I get it.

279
00:14:49,932 --> 00:14:52,017
And your family gives you love.

280
00:14:52,100 --> 00:14:55,729
You should spend some time
with our kids, Peter. And with me.

281
00:14:55,812 --> 00:14:57,856
What could me and you do together?

282
00:14:57,940 --> 00:14:58,941
[Naughty laugh]

283
00:14:59,483 --> 00:15:01,652
Lois! You've got a sick mind!

284
00:15:01,735 --> 00:15:04,363
Peter, I'm talking about making love.

285
00:15:04,613 --> 00:15:08,242
I thought you wanted us to murder
the children and harvest their organs...

286
00:15:08,325 --> 00:15:09,493
...for beer money.

287
00:15:09,660 --> 00:15:11,036
[Amorous giggling]

288
00:15:14,748 --> 00:15:18,168
What a gorgeous day.
Isn't it a gorgeous day, Mr. Sun?

289
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:21,296
It's always a nice day
with two scoops of raisins, Peter.

290
00:15:23,298 --> 00:15:24,299
[Car alarm blaring]

291
00:15:25,926 --> 00:15:28,345
-Top of the morning, everybody.
-Excellent!

292
00:15:28,428 --> 00:15:31,849
Thus completes the penultimate
adjustment to my weather control device!

293
00:15:31,932 --> 00:15:34,184
Victory is.... Release me at once!

294
00:15:34,268 --> 00:15:38,564
Your mother was right. It'd be a crime
to sit around and wait for the TV.

295
00:15:38,647 --> 00:15:40,899
Great. You can teach me how to drive.

296
00:15:40,983 --> 00:15:43,235
There'll be time to drive
when you're dead.

297
00:15:43,318 --> 00:15:46,613
There's a world out there waiting
for us to grab it by the short hairs!

298
00:15:46,697 --> 00:15:47,948
-Damn!
-Let's go.

299
00:15:48,824 --> 00:15:50,868
[Cheery instrumental music]

300
00:16:26,069 --> 00:16:29,781
I'm so tired. This morning's fly-fishing
really wore me out.

301
00:16:29,865 --> 00:16:33,285
Wake up! You promised you'd get
this hook out of my mouth.

302
00:16:33,368 --> 00:16:34,411
[Screams]

303
00:16:34,494 --> 00:16:35,495
Thank you.

304
00:16:35,579 --> 00:16:39,082
Now, kids, your father's just trying
to spend time with his family.

305
00:16:39,625 --> 00:16:42,002
Or kill us. I'm not sure which.

306
00:16:42,294 --> 00:16:44,505
TOM: The Chinese sure like to spit,
don't they?

307
00:16:44,588 --> 00:16:47,883
Diane, that last report was so good,
I think you deserve a spanking.

308
00:16:47,966 --> 00:16:50,052
I don't think your wife
would appreciate that.

309
00:16:50,135 --> 00:16:53,680
That frigid old cow lives in Quahog.
She can't hear a word I'm saying.

310
00:16:53,764 --> 00:16:56,642
Actually, we're back on the air in Quahog.

311
00:16:59,311 --> 00:17:00,312
STEWIE: Thank God!

312
00:17:00,395 --> 00:17:04,316
Their puerile minds are once again
distracted by that flickering box.

313
00:17:04,399 --> 00:17:05,984
Time to be bad!

314
00:17:08,862 --> 00:17:09,863
PETER: Come on, everyone.

315
00:17:09,947 --> 00:17:13,075
We're late for the Bavarian Folk Festival.
You know those Germans.

316
00:17:13,158 --> 00:17:15,244
You don't join their party,
they come get you.

317
00:17:15,327 --> 00:17:17,371
But Dad, the TV's back on.

318
00:17:18,163 --> 00:17:20,082
What do you know? Okay, let's go.

319
00:17:20,165 --> 00:17:23,794
Peter, I'm thrilled that you want to spend
so much time with the family.

320
00:17:23,877 --> 00:17:25,629
But we're exhausted.

321
00:17:26,046 --> 00:17:28,882
Maybe we could just sit
and watch some TV together?

322
00:17:28,966 --> 00:17:31,844
We're too busy living life to the fullest.
Come on, let's go.

323
00:17:31,927 --> 00:17:34,847
-I'm sick of life.
-Yeah. My dogs are barking.

324
00:17:34,930 --> 00:17:36,932
-But I thought we were having fun.
-We were.

325
00:17:37,015 --> 00:17:41,061
But now it might be nice to watch
other people have fun or get killed.

326
00:17:41,144 --> 00:17:45,190
-You know, whatever's on.
-Look, Peter. It's your favorite show.

327
00:17:46,525 --> 00:17:49,987
This is a dangerous mission.
And it's likely one of us will be killed.

328
00:17:50,070 --> 00:17:54,157
The landing party will consist of myself,
Mr. Spock, Dr. McCoy, and Ensign Rickey.

329
00:17:54,241 --> 00:17:55,367
Crap.

330
00:17:55,450 --> 00:17:56,451
Sorry, Lois.

331
00:17:56,535 --> 00:17:59,621
There's only one show I want to see.
It's called...

332
00:17:59,705 --> 00:18:03,458
...Make Every Day Count,
starring Peter Griffin as himself.

333
00:18:03,542 --> 00:18:07,296
LOIS: Come on, Peter.
Don't you miss TV just a little?

334
00:18:07,379 --> 00:18:11,967
The familiar stories, the broadly drawn
characters, the convenient plot turns...

335
00:18:12,050 --> 00:18:15,846
...that bring a character around
at exactly the right moment?

336
00:18:16,221 --> 00:18:18,390
Hi. I'm William Shatner.
My car broke down...

337
00:18:18,473 --> 00:18:21,685
...on my way to give a speech
on how TV keeps families together.

338
00:18:21,768 --> 00:18:22,769
Would you like to hear it?

339
00:18:22,853 --> 00:18:25,856
No, I don't want to miss
the all-you-can-eat schnitzel bar.

340
00:18:25,939 --> 00:18:28,066
Wait a minute! I love schnitzel!

341
00:18:28,150 --> 00:18:31,153
Come along. I bet you could squeeze
into Lois' lederhosen.

342
00:18:31,236 --> 00:18:33,197
I'll change in the car.

343
00:18:34,865 --> 00:18:37,910
If I had a nickel for every time
one of my parents walked out...

344
00:18:37,993 --> 00:18:41,246
...instead of teaching me how to drive,
I'd be one rich little--

345
00:18:41,330 --> 00:18:42,831
Let's go, Meg.

346
00:18:43,665 --> 00:18:46,210
[Sinister instrumental music]

347
00:19:04,394 --> 00:19:06,063
Fare thee well, broccoli!

348
00:19:06,313 --> 00:19:08,398
[Band playing German folk music]

349
00:19:20,327 --> 00:19:23,330
I don't know. I can't imagine
choosing life over television.

350
00:19:23,413 --> 00:19:25,332
I'm telling you, it's great, Bill.

351
00:19:25,415 --> 00:19:27,709
The only thing that would make this

352
00:19:27,793 --> 00:19:30,087
perfect day better is if
my family was here.

353
00:19:31,255 --> 00:19:32,256
My God!

354
00:19:32,339 --> 00:19:34,550
It was sunny a moment ago,
but now it's pouring!

355
00:19:34,633 --> 00:19:36,760
Let's take off our shoes
and run home barefoot!

356
00:19:36,844 --> 00:19:39,263
Griffin, you're a madman!
Barefoot, you say?

357
00:19:39,346 --> 00:19:40,472
LOIS: This is not safe.

358
00:19:40,597 --> 00:19:43,475
I'll teach you how to drive
some other time.Pull over.

359
00:19:43,559 --> 00:19:45,644
Mom, I can't even tell where "over" is.

360
00:19:46,019 --> 00:19:47,729
[Giddy laughter]

361
00:19:51,108 --> 00:19:53,735
You were right, Peter.
I've never felt so alive.

362
00:19:54,278 --> 00:19:55,445
Victory is mine!

363
00:19:55,529 --> 00:19:56,530
[Screams]

364
00:19:59,950 --> 00:20:01,368
STEWIE: God damn it.

365
00:20:03,203 --> 00:20:04,705
[Giddy laughter]

366
00:20:08,584 --> 00:20:09,793
My God.

367
00:20:11,461 --> 00:20:12,796
[Car colliding]

368
00:20:13,547 --> 00:20:15,841
My God. I hit William Shatner.

369
00:20:16,133 --> 00:20:20,929
Light growing dimmer.
Can't breathe. Beam me up, God.

370
00:20:23,265 --> 00:20:25,058
I did not see that coming.

371
00:20:27,102 --> 00:20:30,564
Daddy, I'm sorry I ran you over
and killed Mr. Shatner.

372
00:20:30,647 --> 00:20:35,402
Don't worry. Once I'm of this body cast,
I'll do enough living for me and Bill.

373
00:20:35,819 --> 00:20:38,906
Honey, can't we go back
to the way things used to be?

374
00:20:38,989 --> 00:20:41,825
There's a big dent in that couch
that nobody else can fill.

375
00:20:41,909 --> 00:20:43,869
Haven't you guys learned anything?

376
00:20:43,952 --> 00:20:47,164
TV took over my life once.
I'm never gonna let that happen again.

377
00:20:47,623 --> 00:20:48,790
My God.

378
00:20:49,499 --> 00:20:50,959
We've lost him.

379
00:20:52,836 --> 00:20:55,547
If you help me out of here,
I know a meadow where...

380
00:20:55,631 --> 00:20:57,674
...the blueberries are begging
to be picked.

381
00:20:57,758 --> 00:20:59,927
Look, buddy. Just go in the pan.

382
00:21:00,010 --> 00:21:02,137
And don't call me
unless you're flatlining.

383
00:21:02,763 --> 00:21:05,098
PETER: Turn that TV off. Nurse?

384
00:21:06,266 --> 00:21:08,602
ANNOUNCER: What would you do
for a Klondike Bar?

385
00:21:08,685 --> 00:21:11,104
ANNOUNCER: Would you stand on one leg?
MAN: Sure.

386
00:21:13,232 --> 00:21:15,067
ANNOUNCER:
Would you act like a monkey?

387
00:21:18,987 --> 00:21:20,739
ANNOUNCER: Would you kill a man?

388
00:21:23,617 --> 00:21:24,618
[Gunshot]

389
00:21:28,372 --> 00:21:31,708
Daddy, now that I've finally passed
my driver's test...

390
00:21:31,792 --> 00:21:34,086
...can I still get a convertible?

391
00:21:34,169 --> 00:21:37,339
No. But I'm proud of you
for getting your license, sweetheart.

392
00:21:37,506 --> 00:21:41,385
And I'm proud of you, Peter.
You taught us all a valuable lesson.

393
00:21:41,468 --> 00:21:44,805
It's not what you do
that defines the quality of your life...

394
00:21:44,888 --> 00:21:47,599
...it's who you do it with,
and your family--

395
00:21:47,683 --> 00:21:48,684
It's on.

396
00:21:51,520 --> 00:21:54,523
I know you don't like broccoli, Stewie,
but you'll thank me...

397
00:21:54,606 --> 00:21:57,067
...when you grow up big and strong
like your father.

398
00:21:57,150 --> 00:22:00,153
A compelling argument.
You've swayed me, woman.

399
00:22:01,113 --> 00:22:04,199
That is good. I feel stronger already.

400
00:22:04,867 --> 00:22:06,952
It's good tasting and good for you.

401
00:22:09,079 --> 00:22:10,080
Nice try.

402
00:22:10,163 --> 00:22:11,623
-Quadruped.
-Mutant.

403
00:22:12,165 --> 00:22:13,709
[Theme music]
